    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70483" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νευρ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>suffering from contraction of the tendons,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. καὶ ἀρθριτικοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antyll.
				</span></i>
			 ap.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				9.11.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.420
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the
			disease itself, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. διάθεσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					331.11
				</span></i>
			 (Pergam., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				<i>like a tendon,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ruf.
					<u>Syn.Puls.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			.</div>
